--TEST--
an in-process request whose program throws and does not catch answers `500` and an empty body, whatever it declared and wrote first, and one that catches its own throw keeps both — `rule:testing/in-process-request`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Test\Response::status, Core\Test\Response::body
//
// The server answers a failed request `500` with no body (`nvs-server`'s
// `answer`), so a test must see the same, or a test of an error path passes
// while production fails. Both sides of the bound in one run: the program that
// catches its own throw still answers what it declared and wrote.
//
// The `catch (LogicError ...)` is the parent: there is no request in its run.
try {
    var $path = Core\Request::path();
    Core\Response::setStatus(201);
    echo "half a page";
    if ($path == "/caught") {
        try {
            throw new RuntimeError("handled");
        } catch (RuntimeError $handled) {
            echo " and the rest";
        }
    } else {
        throw new RuntimeError("not handled");
    }
} catch (LogicError $noRequest) {
    var $failed = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/fails");
    echo "fails ", $failed->status(), " [", $failed->body(), "]\n";
    var $caught = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/caught");
    echo "caught ", $caught->status(), " [", $caught->body(), "]\n";
}
--EXPECT--
fails 500 []
caught 201 [half a page and the rest]
